<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  com.claude.dispatcher — the L4 dispatcher spine (T-P7-4/5): cron-woken `cc-dispatch --once`
  pulls open backlog items → quota-places via cc-wave-plan → claims + spawns a worker session,
  logging each decision to the IDL. A quota-cliff PAGES + abstains (never a blind spawn).

  ⚠️  TEMPLATE — NOT auto-loaded. RunAtLoad is FALSE and this file ships UNLOADED on purpose:
  autonomous "Claude kicks off Claude" spawning begins ONLY when the OPERATOR loads it by hand
  (launchctl bootstrap) after the C10 review in docs/activation/dispatcher-activate-snippet.md.
  The agent never loads launchd. Kill-switch: `launchctl bootout gui/$UID/com.claude.dispatcher`.

  MIGRATED TO CLOUD-ONLY 2026-08-11 (operator directive: "fully migrate cc-backlog from local spawn
  to cloud spawn"). Three exports, and they are one decision:
    CC_FIRE_CLOUD=on            lifts handoff-fire's default-off refusal of the off-box venue
    CC_DISPATCH_VENUE_ONLY=cloud admits ONLY venuePlan=cloud rows; everything else is parked and
                                COUNTED in the IDL every pass (bin/cc-dispatch 1a1)
    (DECIDE_ONLY removed)       the pause below is superseded — it stopped cloud spawns too, which
                                is why the migration needed a venue filter rather than a lift
  ✅ INTERLOCK DISCHARGED 2026-08-11T19:0xZ — all four steps done, step 3 by POSITIVE CONTROL:
  with the pause still on, one pass through the DEPLOYED binary journalled
  `venue-only=cloud parked 272 of 315 dispatchable item(s)` and fired 0 local panes. Only then was
  CC_DISPATCH_DECIDE_ONLY removed. The history below is kept because it is why the order exists.

  🚨 THE INTERLOCK, AND IT COST A REAL BLEED TO LEARN (2026-08-11). DECIDE_ONLY had to stay on
  until the DEPLOYED binary honoured CC_DISPATCH_VENUE_ONLY. The flip
  was attempted as a pure config change and it fired 2 LOCAL panes: `~/.claude/bin/cc-dispatch` is a
  per-file symlink into the shared checkout, which trails origin/main, so the running binary had
  never heard of the new variable — it read an env var it does not implement, ignored it, saw the
  pause lifted, and dispatched the local queue. An unknown env var is SILENTLY IGNORED by every
  shell program; there is no arity error to catch this.
  THE ORDER IS THEREFORE MECHANICAL, NOT A PREFERENCE:
    1. land the filter                     2. converge the live layer (scripts/deploy-live.sh)
    3. PROVE the deployed copy honours it  4. only then remove CC_DISPATCH_DECIDE_ONLY
  Step 3 is a positive control, not a version check: run one pass with VENUE_ONLY set against a
  queue that HAS local rows and assert the IDL carries `venue-only=... parked N of M`. Absence of
  that record is the signature of the bleed above — a filter that is not there looks exactly like a
  filter with nothing to do (MEMORY.md: deployed-layer-bootstrap-circle, and the cloud pipeline's
  own defect #2: "a rail must call the siblings it shipped with").

  🚨 THE COST, MEASURED AT THE FLIP AND NOT AN ESTIMATE: 45 cloud / 236 local / 31 unlabelled of 312
  dispatchable rows, so 267 items — 86% of the queue — will NOT fire while this stands. That is
  inherent, not a tuning problem: the VM gets a shallow 50-commit clone, no gh, and no ~/.claude, so
  cc-eligible refuses most work BY MEASUREMENT (ineligible-box 155, spawn-rail 24, branch-banking
  25, visual 16, deep-history 15, offbox-lane 10). Raising the migrated share means changing what
  the VM can reach, never loosening the predicate — a wrong answer in a venue nobody can SEE is the
  anti-goal CLOUD_BACKLOG_PIPELINE.md §5 names.
  ROLLBACK is a config change, not a code change: CC_DISPATCH_VENUE_ONLY=local restores the old
  behaviour for the local queue; deleting the export restores both venues.

  SUPERSEDED — PAUSED TO DECIDE-ONLY 2026-08-11 (kept: it is why the venue filter exists).
  CC_DISPATCH_DECIDE_ONLY=on made every
  pass journal its decisions and take ZERO claims, spawns and pages — cc-dispatch calls this "the
  safe activation lane" at :1326. Two reasons, both measured that day:
    1. CAPACITY. 189 worker panes fired in one day against an operator budget of ~15 concurrent
       sessions. The box sat at 2.19 load/core against handoff-fire's own 2.0 ceiling, which
       REFUSED this session's fire — the dispatcher was competing with the operator for the fleet.
    2. STALENESS. Nothing yet gates an item on being current at the moment it FIRES. cc-premise
       re-runs a stored falsifier at claim time, but coverage is 51.5% and it deliberately advises
       rather than refuses, so ~half of dispatchable rows can fire a brief written against a tree
       that has since moved. The readiness conjunction that closes this is filed, not built:
       docs/plans/BACKLOG_CONSOLIDATION_2026-08-09.md section READINESS, waves d73a772a8468 /
       0e8a10c501af / df003b95630b.
  Store hygiene is UNAFFECTED and that is why this lever was chosen over a bootout: the decide pass
  still runs step 1d, retracting stale plan-open items, and still journals every decision — so the
  backlog keeps converging while nothing spawns.
  REVERT: delete the export, reinstall, `launchctl bootout` + `bootstrap`. Do that only once the
  readiness gate is enforcing, or the two reasons above are both still true.

  StartInterval 300s (5 min): the BACKSTOP, not the primary clock (AUTONOMY_DISPATCH_V2 §3 S5).
  `cc-backlog add` kicks a debounced decision pass on write, so the common path is seconds; this
  timer is what GUARANTEES the 5-minute decision bound (§7 A2) even with the kick disabled
  (CC_BACKLOG_KICK=off) or failing. Was 900s, which alone could not meet that bound.
  PATH prepends ~/.claude/bin so cc-dispatch, cc-backlog, cc-wave-plan, handoff-fire.sh + jq
  resolve (launchd's default PATH lacks it — the 36f9d64 lesson). $HOME expands at runtime.

  CC_DISPATCH_PROJECT is the PINNED project, not the only one. DO NOT edit it to add a project and
  DO NOT add a second instance of this job per project (item f7abcbdee98c): the dispatch set is
  {this value} ∪ {scripts/dispatch-projects.conf rows with repo=}, so adding a project is ONE line
  in that conf file with no bootout/bootstrap cycle. Per-project launchd instances were rejected
  because they share the singleton pass lock (mutual pass-in-flight skips), multiply the fleet
  concurrency ceiling (live_workers is a GLOBAL claimed fold), and make coverage an operator action
  per project — full rationale in the DISPATCH SET header block of bin/cc-dispatch.

  This comment is documentation only: launchd-parity-lint compares `plutil -p` output, which does
  not include XML comments, so editing this block cannot drift the repo SSOT from the live plist
  (verified 2026-07-29).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.claude.dispatcher</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>-c</string>
        <string>export PATH="$HOME/.claude/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin"; export CC_DISPATCH_PROJECT="claude-infrastructure"; export CC_FIRE_CLOUD=on; export CC_DISPATCH_VENUE_ONLY=cloud; exec "$HOME/.claude/bin/cc-dispatch" --once</string>
    </array>

    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>300</integer>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>

    <key>LowPriorityIO</key>
    <true/>

    <key>Nice</key>
    <integer>5</integer>

    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/claude-dispatcher.stdout.log</string>

    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/claude-dispatcher.stderr.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
